repository-code: "https://github.com/LucasAlves8Sp/THE-INVERSE-PROBLEM-FOR-THE-NUMBER-OF-CONNECTED-INDUCED-SUBGRAPHS"
abstract: >-
  For a finite graph G, let c(G) be the number of nonempty vertex sets that induce a connected
  subgraph. A positive integer k equals c(G) for some finite connected graph G if and only if
  k is not in {2, 4, 5, 8, 9, 16}. Every attainable value k other than 25 is attained on
  floor(log2 k) + 1 vertices, the least possible number, and 25 needs six vertices. The proofs use
  no computer and are formalized in Lean 4.
